cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Folklore Clinical Variant Interpretation MCP, please cite this
  software using the metadata below.
title: Folklore Clinical Variant Interpretation MCP
type: software
authors:
  - name: Helena Bioinformatics
    website: https://helena.bio
version: 1.4.0
date-released: 2026-08-27
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21922951
url: https://folklore.helena.bio
repository-code: https://github.com/helena-bioinformatics/folklore-mcp
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - clinical variant interpretation
  - genomics
  - bioinformatics
  - ACMG/AMP
  - Model Context Protocol
  - germline variants
abstract: >-
  The official public, read-only Model Context Protocol adapter for Folklore.
  It gives AI clients structured access to public germline variant evidence,
  automated ACMG/AMP decision support, provenance, variant literature, and
  semantic search across a public scientific Literature Corpus.
  The adapter accepts no patient, phenotype, family, or case context. Folklore's
  proprietary interpretation backend and evidence database are not included.
references:
  - type: generic
    title: Public germline variant interpretation contract benchmark
    url: https://github.com/helena-bioinformatics/folklore-mcp/tree/main/benchmarks/variant-interpretation
  - type: generic
    title: Neutral comparison method for automated ACMG/AMP tools
